<title>DENMARK: Danish February reserves fall to 95.7 bln Dkk.</title>
<headline>Danish February reserves fall to 95.7 bln Dkk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's foreign exchange reserves fell to 95.7 billion crowns at end-February 1997 from 96.3 billion crowns at end-January, according to the central bank's monthly balance sheet released on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH RESERVES</p>
<p>				  Feb 1997    Jan 1997    Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Reserves (bln crowns)    95.7	 96.30	 76.5</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement, the central bank said its foreign loan transactions had been broadly in balance in February. Five analysts polled by Reuters had an average prediction that Denmark's foreign reserves would fall to 95.4 billion crowns ($14.6 billion) in February.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652 ($ = 6.514 Danish Crowns)</p>
